# 1️⃣ Subsets

## 📖 Problem

Generate all possible subsets (Power Set) of an array.

---

### Example

Input

```text
[1,2,3]
```

Output

```text
[]

[1]

[2]

[3]

[1,2]

[1,3]

[2,3]

[1,2,3]
```

---

### Approach

```
Choose element

↓

Include

↓

Exclude

↓

Repeat
```

---

### Time Complexity

```
O(2ⁿ)
```

---

# 2️⃣ Subsequences

## 📖 Problem

Generate all possible subsequences of a sequence.

---

### Example

Input

```text
ABC
```

Output

```text
""

A

B

C

AB

AC

BC

ABC
```

---

### Observation

Each character has two choices.

```
Take

or

Not Take
```

---

### Time Complexity

```
O(2ⁿ)
```

---

# 3️⃣ Permutations

## 📖 Problem

Generate all possible arrangements of elements.

---

### Example

Input

```text
1 2 3
```

Output

```text
123

132

213

231

312

321
```

---

### Approach

```
Choose one element

↓

Mark Visited

↓

Recursively build answer

↓

Backtrack
```

---

### Time Complexity

```
O(N!)
```

---

# 4️⃣ Combination Sum

## 📖 Problem

Find all combinations whose sum equals the target.

---

### Example

Input

```text
Candidates

2 3 6 7

Target

7
```

Output

```text
[2,2,3]

[7]
```

---

### Approach

```
Choose Current Number

↓

Reuse

or

Skip

↓

Continue
```

---

### Time Complexity

```
Exponential
```

---

# 5️⃣ N-Queens Problem

## 📖 Problem

Place N queens on an N × N chessboard such that no two queens attack each other.

---

### Rules

Queens cannot attack

```
Same Row

Same Column

Diagonal
```

---

### Example

```
Q . . .

. . Q .

. Q . .

. . . Q
```

---

### Approach

```
Place Queen

↓

Check Safe Position

↓

Recursive Call

↓

Remove Queen
```

---

### Time Complexity

```
O(N!)
```

---

# 6️⃣ Rat in a Maze

## 📖 Problem

Find all possible paths from the top-left corner to the bottom-right corner.

---

### Allowed Moves

```
Up

Down

Left

Right
```

---

### Approach

```
Current Cell

↓

Mark Visited

↓

Explore All Directions

↓

Unmark Cell
```

---

### Time Complexity

```
O(4^(N²))
```

---

# 7️⃣ Sudoku Solver

## 📖 Problem

Fill the Sudoku grid following Sudoku rules.

---

### Rules

Each row contains

```
1–9
```

Each column contains

```
1–9
```

Each 3×3 box contains

```
1–9
```

---

### Approach

```
Find Empty Cell

↓

Try 1–9

↓

Check Validity

↓

Recursive Call

↓

Undo
```

---

### Time Complexity

```
Exponential
```

---

# 8️⃣ Word Search

## 📖 Problem

Determine whether a word exists in a character grid.

---

### Example

```
A B C E

S F C S

A D E E
```

Target

```
ABCCED
```

Output

```
True
```

---

### Approach

```
Choose Cell

↓

DFS

↓

Mark Visited

↓

Undo
```

---

### Time Complexity

```
O(N × M × 4^L)

L = Length of Word
```

---

# 9️⃣ Palindrome Partitioning

## 📖 Problem

Partition a string such that every substring is a palindrome.

---

### Example

Input

```
aab
```

Output

```
[a,a,b]

[aa,b]
```

---

### Approach

```
Choose Substring

↓

Check Palindrome

↓

Recursive Call

↓

Backtrack
```

---

### Time Complexity

```
O(2ⁿ)
```

---

